      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div class="bbWrapper">I&#039;m sure you&#039;ve seen this topic pop up around the interwebs the in the last couple days...here is my take on it:<br />
<br />
Fender, like most large guitar manufacturers, makes most of their money on their lower-priced instruments and they are getting hammered by Chinese counterfeits and copies sold on AliExpress, Temu et al. The Strat shape is public domain in the USA and China doesn&#039;t protect IP, so the logical place to sue is in the EU, specifically Germany as it is the biggest guitar market there...<br />
<br />
<a href="https://thegearforum.com/threads/fender-is-threatening-strat-style-manufacturers-in-germany-with-cease-desist.11393/" class="link link--internal">Read more</a></div>]]></content:encoded>
      <slash:comments>799</slash:comments>
    </item>
